{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"lov_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Loveless\n*Haraway's Dog*","x":-1200,"y":-2320,"width":260,"height":80,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cv_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Camus + Vinck\n*Unfolding Digital Materiality*","x":780,"y":-2320,"width":300,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"lov_dog","type":"text","text":"**The Dog**\nYour entry point into research is much more a *relation* than it is any specific topic. The specific, non-generalizable tangle of curiosity, body, and material that you choose to follow. Research begins with a commitment. And that commitment leads immediately to question(s).","x":-1560,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lov_situated","type":"text","text":"**Situated Knowledge**\nHaraway: there is no view from nowhere. All knowledge is partial, located, embodied. The fiction of objectivity is a way of hiding whose body is doing the knowing.","x":-1200,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lov_rc","type":"text","text":"**Research-Creation**\nLoveless extends this into practice: the work you make is not separate from the knowing. Making *is* the method. The dog is what keeps you honest about what you are actually inside of.","x":-840,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cv_digital","type":"text","text":"**Digital as Material**\nDigital objects are not immaterial. Code, data, and interfaces have weight — they break down, resist, accumulate friction. Camus + Vinck insist on treating digital things as *things*, with their own agencies and constraints.","x":740,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cv_scripts","type":"text","text":"**Scripts and Prescriptions**\nEvery digital tool has a script — a built-in theory of use. The tool prescribes what counts as valid input, valid action, valid output. To use the tool is to partially accept its script.","x":1100,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cv_entangle","type":"text","text":"**Material-Digital Entanglement**\nThe digital does not float above the physical — it is entangled with it. Hardware, software, bodies, and environments co-constitute what the system can and cannot do.","x":1460,"y":-2060,"width":300,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dq1","type":"text","text":"What is the relation — not the topic — that you are already committed to? What keeps pulling you back before you even have a research question?","x":-1040,"y":-1100,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq2","type":"text","text":"Where in your signal chain does a tool's script conflict with what your material is actually doing? What gets lost in that translation?","x":-600,"y":-1100,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq3","type":"text","text":"Is your knowledge claim about the material, or about what happens to the material when your apparatus touches it? Can you tell the difference?","x":-140,"y":-1100,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq4","type":"text","text":"What is one thing your tools assume that you have stopped questioning? How does that assumption shape what your project can become?","x":300,"y":-1100,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq5","type":"text","text":"Whose body was imagined when your primary tool was designed? Are you working inside that imagination or against it?","x":740,"y":-1100,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"convergence","type":"text","text":"### Design Your Constraints\nYou are not starting from zero. You have a body, a history, a set of tools, and a relation you keep returning to. The proposal is meant to be a a plan for what you will do. It is meant to be the constraints you setup in order to practice within and make artifacts.\n\n*Name it. Commit to it. Design from there.*","x":-360,"y":-820,"width":760,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cross_constraint","type":"text","text":"**Enabling constraints as situated commitments.**\nA constraint is not a limitation you impose from outside. It is an honest acknowledgment of what you are already inside.","x":-100,"y":-1340,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cross_specificity","type":"text","text":"**Both texts agree on specificity.**\nLoveless: the dog cannot be generalized. Camus + Vinck: the digital thing cannot be abstracted from its material conditions. You cannot research, make, or build *in general*.","x":-160,"y":-1920,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cross_script_dog","type":"text","text":"**The script is part of the dog.**\nIf your entry point is a material process, the tools you use to sense and process it are participants in that observation. They have prior understanding. They have scripts. In this way, your dog is already entangled with them.","x":-240,"y":-1620,"width":440,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Week 04 — Design Enabling Constraints\n*What is your dog? Loveless, Haraway, and the specificity of situated knowledge. Proposal workshopping.*","x":-240,"y":-2720,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"39a77df71e46f842","type":"text","text":"> [!quote] Languages (discourses) precede us; research methods and disciplines precede us. We enter into them and they work to craft the possible forms of our questions. Thus, when examining our research practices, it is crucial to ask: which stories are animating our choices? Why might this research choice *matter*? Alternate (research) stories create alternate (research) worlds. Conversely, different storytelling strategies (methods and practices) emerge from different worldviews and commitments. ","x":-2400,"y":-2260,"width":576,"height":220},
		{"id":"0b36321b0c669de3","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 04 - Design Enabling Constraints/submodules/DIGM 553 - W04A - What Is Your Dog.md","x":-2080,"y":-1400,"width":840,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"subB","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 04 - Design Enabling Constraints/submodules/DIGM 553 - W04B - Speculative Proposal Workshop.md","x":-240,"y":-360,"width":520,"height":380,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"proposal_example","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 04 - Design Enabling Constraints/Documents/Speculative Proposal — Example.md","x":520,"y":-480,"width":520,"height":640,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e366baaef51ab4b2","x":1280,"y":-320,"width":505,"height":233,"type":"text","text":"> [!note] Your Proposal is a Story\n> Not a plan, a story.\n> A story about what you are already committed to and why that commitment matters.\n> Your methods help tell that story."},
		{"id":"a5b7eb9c636b5c5f","x":1900,"y":-1380,"width":699,"height":700,"type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/submodules/DIGM 553 - W03C - Barad — Entanglement and Intra-action.md"},
		{"id":"6c50332e8ca5c43b","x":1500,"y":-1620,"width":236,"height":103,"type":"text","text":"# ***The Matter-Network***"},
		{"id":"23beee6882899f87","x":1200,"y":-920,"width":456,"height":281,"type":"text","text":"> [! Your Signal Chain is a Matter-Network]\n> None of its parts are the \"thing.\" The thing is the set of associations between them, maintained through active labor.\n> The project _is_ its network of relations. Understanding it means following what it connects, not reducing it to what it \"is.\""},
		{"id":"274e138443fe0f6a","x":840,"y":280,"width":520,"height":180,"type":"text","text":"> [!warning] You can consider this proposal as a form of “ethics document,” to echo Loveless. When designing enabling constraints, you are making a claim about what you are willing to foreclose, about the trust around your material/object, and how you are positioning yourself within the research."},
		{"id":"d6f8da372e16279d","x":40,"y":320,"width":530,"height":266,"type":"text","text":"> [!example] The Boundary Object\n> The boundary object gives you the _permission_ to stop trying to force your work fit cleanly into one category/silo.\n> The project that embraces the “boundary object,” can speak to multiple communities (the department, the field, the art world, a grant committee, a future employer, etc.). Giving it much more circulation potential and more staying power.\n\n"},
		{"id":"d73a2ad5eb3f74bf","x":-1707,"y":-529,"width":387,"height":69,"type":"text","text":"# ***Cuts, Boundaries, and Objects***"},
		{"id":"c890c797f414aea8","x":-1720,"y":-360,"width":417,"height":141,"type":"text","text":"**Agential cut** (Barad) is the most fundamental unit: every act of measurement, sensing, or processing enacts a boundary. The CUT produces from a specific context."},
		{"id":"5a1d9e4dddc7a74c","x":-1720,"y":-120,"width":420,"height":134,"type":"text","text":"**Boundary work** (Camus + Vinck) is what agential cuts look like in practice, at the level of technical labor. It's the ongoing, contested, material effort to stabilize an agential cut."},
		{"id":"c59eb388ee46b6a0","x":-1720,"y":120,"width":420,"height":160,"type":"text","text":"**Boundary object** (Bowker + Star via Loveless) operates at the social/institutional scale. Once the cuts have been made and the boundaries have been worked, the resulting artifact circulates across communities that care about different things."},
		{"id":"1d7cf11eef787151","x":-1260,"y":-100,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"Stabilization"},
		{"id":"5330870bc51d9d2a","x":-1260,"y":-340,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"Production"},
		{"id":"4835310e1e4ffe0e","x":-1260,"y":140,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"Circulation"},
		{"id":"621462e984f6d7f2","x":-2040,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"Unsettling"},
		{"id":"864dc32325145e8a","x":-2040,"y":-120,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"5","type":"text","text":"Remixing"},
		{"id":"8b6e79120113783f","x":-2040,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3","type":"text","text":"Embodying"},
		{"id":"6de63c9db35b9cbf","x":-2040,"y":220,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"4","type":"text","text":"Transmitting"},
		{"id":"6f9f24219a6f1b90","x":1480,"y":-20,"width":440,"height":545,"type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 04 - Design Enabling Constraints/Documents/Speculative Proposal — Example.pdf"},
		{"id":"5d1e0363f07e03e0","x":-1520,"y":-2560,"width":528,"height":80,"type":"text","text":"> [!quote] The crafting of a research question is the crafting of a story that is also the crafting of an ethics."}
	],
